  "releaseNotes": "Version 1.5.0 of Zipwire.ProofPack.Ethereum.\n      - Behaviour change: new ES256KJwsSigner(key) now writes the standard JWS signature (RFC 8812), 64 bytes in base64url. Before it wrote the legacy 65-byte form in standard base64.\n      - ES256KSignatureFormat.Jws is base64url too. Pass ES256KSignatureFormat.Ethereum to keep the legacy form.\n      - Tokens from the new default fail on verifiers older than 1.4.0; 1.4.0 verifiers (dotnet and JavaScript) read both.\n      - Requires Zipwire.ProofPack 1.4.0 (unchanged).",
